  "notes": [
    "Retained initial Windows-sys zero-initialization and test fixture path/engine field diagnostics, plus Clippy redundant Box<Arc> and consecutive replace findings. Corrected using explicit valid FFI initializers and a stable Arc callback context, without lint exclusions.",
    "Native registry test initially consumed a queued change snapshot while checking resume. It now drains only already-delivered snapshots before the explicit wake; real read-count assertions remain. All9 privacy tests pass.",
    "Visual harness initially assumed single-activity split width and the generic94px peek. It now asserts existing260+6+32 split geometry and measured78px privacy content. Original compact232x32 layout stays exact.",
    "The first native Peek was correctly auto-dismissed with the fixture cursor outside. Hold only the injected cursor inside the owned Peek for final capture; no OS cursor move, source change or policy weakening. Failed native-a reports/captures remain.",
    "Interim v55-privacy-c captures are preserved. The final layout removes a redundant flex spacer so long app names use the remaining width before truncation; full title tooltips remain. Final acceptance is v55-privacy-d.",
    "The native release is built after the final frontend. Its smoke checks actual embedded entry and all static styles, exact native amber/lime pixels, pushed Peek and hidden alpha.",
    "Previous v51-v54 evidence remains unchanged. No real device, ConsentStore, user app/profile/account, hosted Tack, clipboard/global input, OS clock/power/settings, installer or signing is exercised. Disposable Nabbit-owned registry keys and an owned child test the real Windows notification/wait APIs separately."
